# --- private material never published ---
# Anchored with a leading slash: an unanchored `Legacy/` matches a directory of
# that name at ANY depth, and git on this machine runs with core.ignorecase=true,
# so it silently swallowed app/Actions/Legacy, app/Support/Legacy and
# tests/Fixtures/legacy - the import code itself - while still reporting a clean
# tree. The real dump and the uploads live at the repository root and nowhere
# else, so the root is the only place this has to cover.
/Legacy/
/legacy-review.md
assets/envato/

# --- environment and secrets ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
